{%- comment -%}
  Cart line item — low-stock "Only N left" badge.
  Shared between `sections/main-cart.liquid` and `sections/cart-drawer.liquid`.

  Counts what is still AVAILABLE TO ADD, not gross inventory. The badge used to
  print `variant.inventory_quantity` straight out, so a shopper holding 2 of the
  4 remaining units was told "Only 4 left in your size" — an urgency claim that
  is not true for them, and one that collapses the moment they try to add a fifth
  and the cart refuses. Subtracting what they already hold makes the number the
  one that actually constrains them, and hides the badge entirely once they hold
  the lot: there is nothing left to warn about.

  Uses item_count_for_variant rather than item.quantity so a variant split across
  several lines (hidden properties, bundles) is counted once, in full.

  Params:
    item       (required) — a Shopify cart line item.
    enabled    (required) — bool; render nothing when false.
    threshold  (required) — int; max remaining quantity at which the badge shows.
    style      (optional) — 'calm' shortens the badge to "N left" and drops the
      red, for the drawer's single meta line where it sits beside the size. The
      urgency is in the number; a full red sentence on every line, next to a
      total that is also red, is a lot of alarm for a cart that is going well.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if enabled -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign scarcity_show = false
    if item.variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' and item.variant.inventory_quantity > 0
      assign scarcity_in_cart = cart | item_count_for_variant: item.variant.id
      assign scarcity_left = item.variant.inventory_quantity | minus: scarcity_in_cart
      if scarcity_left > 0 and scarcity_left <= threshold
        assign scarcity_show = true
      endif
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if scarcity_show -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Deliberately NOT a live region. Every badge used to carry aria-live, so a
      cart with six low-stock lines created six competing live regions that all
      re-announced on any re-render. Cart changes are announced once, centrally,
      by the region CartFeedback owns in assets/cart.js.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if style == 'calm' -%}
      <span class="scarcity-badge scarcity-badge--calm text-xs">{{ scarcity_left }} left</span>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="scarcity-badge text-xs">
        <span class="scarcity-dot" aria-hidden="true">&bull;</span>
        Only {{ scarcity_left }} left in your size
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
